# Read by the systemd user manager, so this covers everything launched as a
# unit - which under Plasma is every .desktop app, since KProcessRunner starts
# them as transient app-*@<hex>.service units.
#
# NB: deliberately short. Plasma already sets QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME and the
# cursor/theme variables itself, and duplicating them here only creates a second
# source of truth that can disagree after a Plasma update. The one thing Plasma
# does NOT set is the VA-API driver.
#
# NB: nothing in this repo set LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME before, even though
# packages/gpu-intel.tsv carries intel-media-driver "for VA-API on UHD 620".
# Having the driver installed is not the same as having it selected - verify
# with `vainfo` after a re-login.
#
# NB: and this is now templated because the driver NAME is the other half of
# the same trap. iHD on an AMD card does not fall back and does not warn - it
# fails to load and VA-API is simply gone, so every video decodes on the CPU
# and the only symptom is a hot laptop. The value below follows .gpu, which
# lib/detect.sh reads from the PCI vendor id; scripts/doctor.sh re-reads it
# live and checks `vainfo` actually returns a driver.
{{ if eq .gpu "intel" -}}
LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iHD
{{- else if eq .gpu "amd" -}}
LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=radeonsi
{{- else -}}
# .gpu is {{ .gpu | quote }} - no VA-API driver selected on purpose. Setting a
# name here for a GPU this repo has not been taught would be a guess, and a
# wrong guess is worse than none: unset means libva probes and finds the right
# driver itself, which is the correct behaviour for an unknown card.
{{- end }}
